 /*
- * HISTORY
- * $Log: trap.c,v $
- * Revision 1.1.2.11  1997/10/15  16:34:47  barbou
- * 	When entering a system call, take the "uniproc_antechamber_mutex" before
- * 	contending with system threads on the "uniproc_mutex".
- * 	[1997/10/15  16:09:42  barbou]
- *
- * Revision 1.1.2.10  1997/03/27  18:29:31  barbou
- * 	In catch_exception_raise_state(), synchronize with activation creation
- * 	(see new_thread_activation()), to avoid using an activation before its
- * 	cthread is wired.
- * 	[97/03/27            barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.9  1996/11/22  15:05:52  barbou
- * 	Added more tests to avoid reporting errors on operations on dead
- * 	threads.
- * 	[1996/11/22  14:57:35  barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.8  1996/11/18  18:15:44  barbou
- * 	Forward the exceptions to a debugger if the task exception port has
- * 	been intercepted. Added osfmach3_trap_unwind to restart an exception
- * 	after the debugger's response.
- * 	Disabled  some debugging messages that can occur when Mach threads
- * 	terminate without exiting.
- * 	[1996/11/18  16:53:50  barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.7  1996/11/05  11:39:51  barbou
- * 	Emulate (in fact, ignore) the "out dx,al" instruction (for the X server
- * 	for Mach64 VGA boards).
- * 	[96/11/05            barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.6  1996/10/24  15:55:09  barbou
- * 	First pass at fixing a problem with fake interrupts.
- * 	Don't call do_bottom_half() if some interrupt already in progress.
- * 	[1996/10/24  15:09:17  barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.5  1996/09/26  13:51:29  barbou
- * 	Tolerate a MACH_SEND_INVALID_DEST return from the thread_get_state()
- * 	in serv_callback_fake_interrupt().  This probably indicates that the
- * 	thread has been killed by an outside agent (e.g., a user program that
- * 	calls Mach services directly) so we should allow the signal to be
- * 	delivered anyway to avoid having unkillable processes whose Mach tasks
- * 	no longer exist.
- * 	[1996/09/23  13:59:23  emcmanus]
- * 	[96/09/26            barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.4  1996/09/24  17:07:19  barbou
- * 	Don't deal with task->errno: it's not used.
