- * 	Undid change from a previous submission: in free_area_discard_pages(),
- * 	m_o_discard_reply() needs to be called even if undiscard_count is null.
- * 	Don't print debugging messages when debug variable is 0.
- * 	[1997/09/30  16:34:21  barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.12  1997/09/26  15:31:20  stephen
- * 	Remove unused/bogus ip_compute_csum prototype
- * 	[1997/09/26  15:25:01  stephen]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.11  1997/09/25  14:26:52  gdt
- * 	Tune up to improve performance.
- * 	Fix "grow_again" timers; they weren't waiting at all!
- * 	Don't be so aggressive about freeing Linux buffer cache pages.
- * 	Make "grow_again" timer and number of buffer pages to free be
- * 	user defined (via 'config') constants.
- * 	[1997/09/25  14:25:53  gdt]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.10  1997/02/07  14:33:24  barbou
- * 	Added a compilation option for USE_SILENT_OVERWRITE. Use it by default.
- * 	[1997/02/07  14:06:11  barbou]
- * 
- * Revision 1.1.2.9  1997/01/28  13:27:49  barbou
- * 	Allocate and wire a "zero" page to speed up some user-memory
- * 	zero-padding loops.
- * 	In free_area_discard_pages, deallocate the page if it has been paged-out
- * 	already: this saves some paging space.
- * 	In free_area_mark_used, do a m_o_data_unavailable in advance to save
- * 	a m_o_data_request from the kernel when the page is actually touched.
- * 	[1997/01/28  13:25:16  barbou]
- * 
